      "writtenOn": "2021-11-16T22:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I was testing the new POWER_S4 state I initially missed a transition case (something like POWER_S5S4). What ended up happening was the task would spin forever calling this function but not getting anywhere, and eventually the EC watchdog would kick in and reboot the EC. I decided to go with POWER_G3 here so that even if we got off track, we could potentially salvage things and get to a known state. But there are also arguments to be made that go like \"well if you got here, trying to salvage things may just keep a broken system broken, so better to reboot and hopefully get the whole world consistent again\". \n\nI guess it comes down to whether we think bugs that land us here are likely to be in the critical boot path or not, where watchdogging out and rebooting would lead to an unusable bootlooping machine. I\u0027m inclined to guess yes, and try to salvage state, but I can see it either way.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "45220230_91abaf46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 461,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 461,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "2d835bf603d236698d732168f14f2c85576d1553",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
